    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ad2a7d7a_881dcf03",
        "filename": "runtime/art_method.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1044,
      "author": {
        "id": 1042828
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-07T14:39:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The C++ standard disagrees. Only the field that was most recently assigned to is live, so reading from the other one is technically UB. See https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/union, \"member lifetime\".\n\nAre we otherwise playing by the rules here, or should the hotness count also really be atomic, because it can be concurently accessed?\n\nSo long as this CL doesn\u0027t make us less conforming than we already were, I\u0027m OK.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1044,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 1044,
        "endChar": 91
      },
      "revId": "a63a1380cfa4c1e0419c8affdcc355cd5f7ce54e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0382a53e_fcb61342",
        "filename": "runtime/art_method.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1044,
      "author": {
        "id": 1018108
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-07T14:55:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I remember that in a union of PODs you can safely access the leading members as long as long as they are identical but I don\u0027t remember where to find it in the standard.\n\n    struct A { int x; short y; long z; };\n    struct B { int x; short y; int z; };\n    union U { A a; B b; } u;\n    u.a \u003d getA();\n    short y \u003d u.b.y;  // OK\n    int x \u003d u.b.z;  // UB even if sizeof(int) \u003d\u003d sizeof(long)\n\nOr do I remember it wrong? (There was also something similar about accessing identical initial fields after `reinterpret_cast\u003c\u003e`.)\n\nSo, I would assume that there is some exception for primitive members of a union when they have the same type, even if they are not wrapped in a POD.\n\nThe fields cannot be concurrently accessed in the `LoadClass()` context before we publish the methods through the class. But we do not properly enforce any ordering for the \"publishing\", so it would be good to make the field atomic. However, that\u0027s outside the scope of this CL.",
      "parentUuid": "ad2a7d7a_881dcf03",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1044,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 1044,
        "endChar": 91
      },
      "revId": "a63a1380cfa4c1e0419c8affdcc355cd5f7ce54e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5ba07f64_69ac1f61",
        "filename": "runtime/art_method.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1044,
      "author": {
        "id": 1042828
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-07T15:25:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "wg21.link/n5001 says in [class.union.general] p2: \"If a standard-layout union contains several standard-layout structs that share a common initial sequence (11.4), and if a non-static data member of an object of this standard-layout union type is active and is one of the standard-layout structs, the common initial sequence of any of the standard-layout struct members can be inspected\".\n\nFor some reason it says that in a note, rather than normative text, which I don\u0027t understand.\n\nSo if you used structs containing an int, you are probably OK. But once we really fix this one union member should be int, and the other atomic\u003cint\u003e, so this may not really be useful.\n\nI was more concerned about concurrent accesses to actually udate the hotness counter once the code is running. We can probably get away with ordinary relaxed accesses without CAS, but I think it still needs to be atomic.",
      "parentUuid": "0382a53e_fcb61342",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1044,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 1044,
        "endChar": 91
      },
      "revId": "a63a1380cfa4c1e0419c8affdcc355cd5f7ce54e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6d3d8322_80bcab64",
        "filename": "runtime/art_method.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1044,
      "author": {
        "id": 1018108
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-07T15:39:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I found the relevant text in 11.4/28, so there is no need to repeat it as normative text in 11.5/2.\n\nMaybe we should use just a plain atomic member (not a `union`) and interpret it according to the access flags.",
      "parentUuid": "5ba07f64_69ac1f61",
      "range": {
